<title>GERMANY: West German May industry output falls 0.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German May industry output falls 0.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    May 97     Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -0.4	 +0.4	 +0.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.8	 +3.0	 -2.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		97.1	97.5	 95.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously announced data in parentheses.</p>
<p>The ministry noted that data for April had been revised upwards and announced that May data were likely to be revised downward.</p>
<p>&quot;Because there are considerably fewer working days in May than in April, on the other hand we have to expect that the latest data later will be revised downwards,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     May 97		  Apr 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     84.0	 -8.4     91.7	 +9.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   97.4	 +0.3     97.1	 +0.2</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods  103.3	 +1.3    102.0	 +1.3</p>
<p>	Capital goods     96.8	 -1.0     97.8	 +3.4</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 80.2	 -5.0     84.4	 -9.0</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    93.0	 +2.9     90.4	 -3.4</p>
<p> Energy output	   109.4	 +1.4    107.9	 +1.8</p>
<p> Construction	     87.7	 -7.9     95.2	 -0.7</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-May 97 with Feb-Mar 97:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +0.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-May 97 with Apr-May 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +2.3</p>
<p> Mining				    +1.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +3.7</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +6.2</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +4.5</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	unch</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -2.6</p>
<p> Energy output			   -1.1</p>
<p> Construction			    -8.1</p>
